# Rich Black desktop theme

Unified opaque dark theme for GTK 3/4, Qt 6, and LibreOffice.
Single source of truth is `quickshell/theme/Theme.qml` — every app
color is derived from it, so the bar, GTK, Qt, and LibreOffice chrome
stay in sync. Flat, opaque, monochrome: no gradients, assets, or glows.
Selection/checked/primary fill is light accent with dark text on top.

## How it works

* `desktop-theme/theme_tokens.py` — parses `Theme.qml`; exposes
  `tokens()`, `css(name)` (GTK `rgba` alpha 0..1), `qss(name)`
  (QSS `rgba` alpha 0..255).
* `desktop-theme/generate.py` — `render` (default) regenerates the
  derived files below; `check` fails if (a) generated files drift from
  `Theme.qml`, (b) hand-authored `gtk.css` files contain raw hex or
  `rgba()` literals, or (c) a `@token` used in `gtk.css` is not defined
  in `colors.css`. Exit non-zero on violation.
* `desktop-theme/templates/rich-black.qss.tmpl` — Qt 6 stylesheet
  template; every color/radius is a `{{token}}` placeholder filled at
  render time.
* `desktop-theme/libreoffice/apply.py` plus
  `desktop-theme/libreoffice/rich-black.settings.json` — idempotently
  fuses tokens into
  `~/.config/libreoffice/4/user/registrymodifications.xcu` (backs up to
  `.bak` first). See `desktop-theme/libreoffice/README.md` for details.

Generated files (do not edit by hand; re-render instead):

* `gtk-3.0/colors.css`, `gtk-4.0/colors.css`
* `qt6ct/colors/rich-black.conf`, `qt6ct/qss/rich-black.qss`

Hand-authored files (only place for manual styling):

* `gtk-3.0/gtk.css`, `gtk-4.0/gtk.css` — must use `@rb_*` /
  libadwaita `@-names` only, no literal colors.
* `desktop-theme/templates/rich-black.qss.tmpl`

## Tokens (from Theme.qml)

bg `#070707` (window bg) · base `#0C0C0C` (headerbar/menubar/toolbar/
dialog) · mantle `#111111` (controls & overlays) · surface0 `#161616`
(hover) · surface1 `#1D1D1D` (borders/pressed) · surface2 `#262626`
(handles/strong separators) · text `#F5F5F5` · subtext1 `#A1A1A1` ·
subtext0 `#6F6F6F` · border `#1D1D1D` · focusBorder `#33F5F5F5`
(20% white focus ring) · accent `#D6D6D6` (selection/checked/primary)
· accentMuted `#969696` · scrim `#B0070707` · muted semantic red
`#C59D9D`, green `#A8B6A4`, mauve `#C8C8C8`, teal `#A8B8B8`, pink
`#BDBDBD`, blue `#AAB3BD`, base3 `#F5F5F5`.
Radii: control 12 · chip 7 · card 16 · large 20.
UI font is Noto Sans 10pt; Qt icons use `breeze-dark`.

## Qt 6 wiring

`qt6ct/qt6ct.conf` sets `color_scheme_path=` to
`qt6ct/colors/rich-black.conf` and `stylesheets=` to
`qt6ct/qss/rich-black.qss`; style stays Fusion. Apps need
`QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=qt6ct` (already exported in `~/.profile`).

## LibreOffice

White document page (WYSIWYG) + dark chrome + readable text + dark
monochrome icons. `apply.py` sets `IsAutomaticFontColor=true`, icon
theme `sifr_dark`, `ApplicationAppearance=2` (force dark),
`UseOnlyWhiteDocBackground=true`, `LibreOfficeTheme=1` (enables the
theme engine — it was `0`, which disabled theming and caused the brown
chrome / transparent menus), and a custom `RICH_BLACK`
Application Colors scheme mapped to the tokens above.

## Keeping it in sync

Run from `~/.config`:

1. Edit `quickshell/theme/Theme.qml`.
2. `python3 desktop-theme/generate.py render` — propagate to GTK/Qt 6.
3. `python3 desktop-theme/generate.py check` — verify no drift and no
   raw colors in `gtk.css`.
4. `python3 desktop-theme/libreoffice/apply.py` — push tokens into
   LibreOffice (restart LibreOffice afterwards).
5. Restart apps to pick up changes: GTK reads
   `~/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css` + `~/.config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css` (restart
   the app; restart `xsettingsd` if a running app does not refresh).
   Qt 6 apps need a restart with `QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=qt6ct`.

Limitation: apps that bundle their own toolkit/theme, use
client-side decoration, or ship their own styling may not fully follow
these colors.
